From: Vagus <vagus@nerves>
Subject: [PATCH] builder-next: look up balena-engine-runc for the buildkit executor

The balena fork renames every binary of the multicall bundle
(runc -> balena-engine-runc) and installs no plain "runc", but
builder-next's executor still hardcodes CommandCandidates
{"runc"}. exec.LookPath("runc") then fails AFTER "Daemon has
completed initialization", killing the daemon at startup on any
system that ships only the renamed symlink set (found on the
vagus rpi3_64 Nerves system).

Prefer the renamed binary, keep "runc" as a fallback.
---
--- a/builder/builder-next/executor_linux.go
+++ b/builder/builder-next/executor_linux.go
@@ -60,6 +60,6 @@
 	return runcexecutor.New(runcexecutor.Opt{
 		Root:                filepath.Join(root, "executor"),
-		CommandCandidates:   []string{"runc"},
+		CommandCandidates:   []string{"balena-engine-runc", "runc"},
 		DefaultCgroupParent: cgroupParent,
 		Rootless:            rootless,
 		NoPivot:             os.Getenv("DOCKER_RAMDISK") != "",
